# Legacy /previous-artists paths. The exact-path rules (bare path and
# /single/:slug) now live in astro.config.mjs's `redirects`, which Astro
# APPENDS to this file at build time — keeping them here too produced
# "Duplicate rule for path" and failed `wrangler deploy` outright.
#
# This splat is the one rule with no Astro equivalent: Astro validates that a
# dynamic redirect's destination matches a real route, and the paginated route
# is [...page], so /records/artists/previous/[...rest] is rejected. It stays
# here to catch anything else under /previous-artists.
#
# Note: _redirects IS honoured on Workers Static Assets (the same way _headers
# from this directory is) — it just doesn't fire for routes the Worker renders.
# DEPLOY.md currently claims this file is inert on our targets; that claim is
# stale and is being corrected separately.
/previous-artists/*  /records/artists/previous/:splat  301
